ad9361_init: check every resource and release it on failure; ad9361_remove frees the ADC core;
the sampling frequency setters fail when the clock chain did not apply (as Linux does).

- axi_adc_init() fails ("cf-ad9361-lpc: Status errors", no DATA_CLK from the transceiver) and
  leaves phy->rx_adc NULL; ad9361_init ignored that and dereferenced it in axi_adc_read() and
  ad9361_post_setup(): a data abort. Now -EIO and a clean unwind.
- the GPIO and SPI descriptors (and the ADC core) leaked on every failed init; a caller that
  retries the init leaked them on every attempt. *ad9361_phy is NULL after a failure.
- ad9361_set_rx/tx_sampling_freq ignored the ad9361_set_trx_clock_chain() result and went on to
  the RF bandwidth update and TX quadrature calibration on a half-applied clock chain.

--- a/drivers/rf-transceiver/ad9361/ad9361_api.c	2026-10-29 12:08:06
+++ b/drivers/rf-transceiver/ad9361/ad9361_api.c	2026-10-29 12:08:28
@@ -483,17 +483,30 @@
 
 	phy->pdata->debug_mode = true;
 
